zstd_vendor: use the system zstd when it is found.

qnx-ports' rosbag2 change makes find_package(zstd) REQUIRED on QNX but
passes ament_vendor() SATISFIED ${ZSTD_SATISFIED}, a variable nothing
sets, so zstd_vendor always built its own libzstd.so.1 into the ROS
prefix -- the soname of the zstd component in /usr/local/lib, and QNX's
loader takes whichever comes first on LD_LIBRARY_PATH. Test zstd_FOUND,
as upstream does.

Upstream-Status: QNX-specific (fixes the qnx-ports change)

--- a/zstd_vendor/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/zstd_vendor/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -15,7 +15,7 @@
 endif()
 
 ament_vendor(zstd_vendor
-  SATISFIED ${ZSTD_SATISFIED}
+  SATISFIED ${zstd_FOUND}
   VCS_URL https://github.com/facebook/zstd.git
   VCS_VERSION v1.5.5
   SOURCE_SUBDIR build/cmake
